  "title": "Present tense: -ar",
  "sortOrder": 9,
  "prerequisiteId": "pronouns",
  "explanation": "A regular -ar verb changes the ending, not the stem. Hablar becomes hablo, hablas, habla, hablamos, habláis, and hablan.\n\nHabláis is the Spain form for a group you know. The pronoun is often left out because the ending already says who.",
  "commonMistake": "Using the yo ending for everybody, or forgetting the accent in habláis.",
